[00:18.66] (intro) The night was clear, and the moon was yellow
[00:20.44] And the leaves came tumblin' down. . .
[00:20.58] I was standing on a corner
[00:20.80] When I heard my bull dog bark
[00:24.12] He was barking at two men
[00:25.94] Who were gambling in the dark
[00:29.96] It was Stagger Lee and Billy
[00:32.14] Two men who gambled late
[00:35.70] Stagger Lee threw a seven
[00:37.84] Billy swore that he threw eight
[00:41.24] Stagger Lee he told Billy
[00:44.26] "I can't let you go with that
[00:44.26] You won all o' my money
[00:44.52] And my brand new Stetson hat."
[00:47.78] Stagger Lee started off walking
[00:47.90] Down that old railroad track
[00:47.90] He turned and told Billy
[00:49.72] "Don't be here when I come back"
[00:53.02] Then old Stagger Lee, he went home
[00:56.56] And he got his forty-four
[01:13.88] He said "I'm going down to the barroom
[01:17.42] To pay that debt I owe"
[01:17.62] bridge: Go, Stagger Lee!
[01:18.70] Stagger Lee went to the barroom
[01:34.16] Walked across that barroom floor
[01:35.26] He said, "Now, nobody move"
[01:36.78] And he pulled out his forty-four
[01:39.70] "Oh, Stagger Lee," cried Billy
[01:43.38] "Please don't take my life
[01:44.16] I got three little children
[01:44.16] And a very sickly wife"
[01:44.16] Stagger Lee... shot Billy
[01:44.16] Oh, he shot that poor boy so bad
[01:46.66] Till the bullet went through Billy
[01:48.82] And it broke the bartender's glass.
